             The following checklist is appropriate for a FIRST TIME CAVER
        GOING TO A "BEGINNER'S CAVE" who wants to see what caving is like
        before investing any real money.

        ** LIGHTING
         
                2 heavily constructed, water-proof flashlights.
                Alkaline batteries and spares for each flashlight.
                An extra bulb for each flashlight.
                Short pieces of nylon cord for flashlight wrist loops.
                A small piece of steel wool or sandpaper for cleaning
                  flashlight electrical contacts.
         
                A thick candle.
                Waterproof matches.

        ** FOR YOUR HEAD
         
                A knitted pull-over type hat.
                A hardhat.
                Something to tie up your hair if it's long.

        ** CLOTHING
         
                Multiple thin layers of clothing are best.  If you have a
                  wool shirt or sweater, wear it.  Wool isn't generally
                  good as an outer layer, but you can cover it with
                  something else.  Remember, it is better to wear too
                  much than too little.  Down clothing is useless in a
                  cave.  As soon as it gets wet, it loses its insulating
                  abilities.
                Two pairs of pants, worn one over the other.  Closely
                  woven coveralls are great as an outer layer.
                Gloves.
         
                Have a complete change of dry clothes appropriate for the
                  surface weather.  Pack them in a garbage bag or two to
                  keep them dry.  The bag is also to carry your "muddies"
                  on your way home.  These dry clothes are essential for
                  coming out of a cave in the winter.

        ** FOOTWEAR
         
                Sneakers are marginally acceptable.  Hiking, climbing, or
                  combat boots are much better.
                Heavy socks.  Wool is best.

        ** MISCELLANEOUS
         
                A plastic garbage bag neatly rolled up.
